  trainingSpark: {fileID: 0}
  lessons:
  - chapter: GETTING STARTED
    title: Your people get things done
    description: 'Drag a person onto School, Research Center or Factory to assign
      work.

      Each building holds up to two people.'
    note: Train people. Discover blueprints. Craft upgrades.
  - chapter: TRY IT YOURSELF
    title: Educate your first person
    description: 'Drag the glowing normal person onto School.

      Training costs
      {school} AP.'
    note: Drag the glowing person to the glowing School.
  - chapter: EDUCATED PEOPLE
    title: Your educated person is ready
    description: 'Send your educated person to Research Center.

      They research
      faster and spend less AP.'
    note: 
  - chapter: RESEARCH
    title: Research disaster protection
    description: 'Drag your educated person onto Research Center.

      Research
      creates blueprints for disaster protection.'
    note: 
  - chapter: SEISMIC BLUEPRINT
    title: Choose earthquake protection
    description: 'Select Rail System, the seismic blueprint.

      It helps protect
      houses from earthquakes.'
    note: 
  - chapter: FACTORY BLUEPRINT
    title: Turn a blueprint into an upgrade
    description: 'Drag the seismic blueprint from the Vault to Factory.

      Factory
      uses the plan to make the real upgrade.'
    note: 
  - chapter: FACTORY PEOPLE
    title: Assign a person to Factory
    description: 'Drag the glowing fresh person onto Factory.

      This job costs
      {normalFactory} AP and produces two seismic items.'
    note: 
  - chapter: READY
    title: Your seismic upgrades are ready
    description: 'Next, drag these items onto any two houses you choose.

      Watch
      each upgrade in the 3D city.'
    note: 
  - chapter: PROTECT HOUSES
    title: Protect the houses you choose
    description: 'Drag each seismic item onto a different house.

      Watch the
      3D installation after each upgrade.'
    note: 
  - chapter: READY
    title: Face the earthquake
    description: 'When you run out of AP or feel ready, press READY

      to end
      your turn and face the disaster.'
    note: 
  - chapter: AP REWARDS
    title: Protected houses earn AP
    description: '{safeHouses} protected houses x {houseReward} AP = {survivalReward}
      AP.

      Round bonus: {roundBonus} AP. Total earned: +{earnedAP} AP.'
    note: 
  - chapter: NEXT DISASTER
    title: Protect every house to move on
    description: 'Make all four houses earthquake-resistant.

      When every house
      survives, you can face the next disaster.'
    note: 
  trainingDescription: 'School is educating this person.

    Wait for the educated
    person to return.'
  trainingNote: No extra AP is spent while training.
  researchingDescription: 'Research is creating a blueprint.

    Wait for the blueprint
    choices to appear.'
  blueprintArrivalDescription: 'Your seismic blueprint is moving to the Vault.

    Wait
    for it to arrive, then drag it to Factory.'
  producingDescription: 'Factory is producing the physical seismic upgrades.

    Wait
    for your two items to arrive.'
